summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Left elbow pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Anna Diaz is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, who presents with left elbow pain.

The patient states she has been having pain in her left elbow for the past few weeks. She works at a desk all day at work and stays in a fixed position. After work, she has trouble opening and closing her left elbow. She has swelling on the tip of her elbow, on the left side. She is right handed, so this is her non-dominant hand. She is still able to write, which is good. Her left elbow is stiff, and it hurts. She denies any numbness or tingling in her hands. She has a little bit of weakness in her arm, but nothing significant. She denies any fever or chills.

Regarding her epilepsy, she has not had any recent seizures. She believes her last seizure was 1 year ago. She is still taking Keppra.

Regarding her depression, she is doing well with therapy. She has been seeing a therapist and has been doing well. She is not interested in starting medication at this time.

Regarding her peptic ulcer disease, she has not had any issues since she underwent an endoscopy 1 year ago. She has been doing well on Protonix.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fevers, chills.
• Musculoskeletal: Endorses left elbow pain. Endorses weakness in her arm.
• Neurological: Denies numbness or tingling in her hands.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.
• Cardiovascular: No murmurs, gallops, or rubs. No extra heart sounds.
• Musculoskeletal: Examination of the left elbow: Erythema and edema of the left elbow. Pain to palpation of the olecranon. Warm to palpation. Pain with flexion and extension of the left elbow. There is a palpable left radial pulse.

RESULTS

X-ray of the left elbow is unremarkable. No evidence of elbow fracture.

Endoscopy showed gastritis.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Anna Diaz is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, who presents with left elbow pain.

Epilepsy.
• Medical Reasoning: She has been doing well since her last seizure 1 year ago.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Keppra 500 mg twice daily.

Depression.
• Medical Reasoning: She is doing well with therapy.
• Medical Treatment: Start Lexapro 10 mg once daily.

Peptic ulcer disease.
• Medical Reasoning: She had an episode of gastritis 1 year ago, which resolved with Protonix.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg once daily before meals.

Left elbow pain.
• Medical Reasoning: This is likely olecranon bursitis secondary to repetitive trauma.
• Medical Treatment: Meloxicam 15 mg once daily. Ice the area.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.
 }}<|eot_id|>
