summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

High blood sugar.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Hannah Davis is a 52-year-old female who presents for evaluation of a high blood sugar.

The patient was in the emergency room with a high blood sugar. She has been eating a lot of sweets recently with the holidays. She feels like there is always something sweet available at work or when she visits her family. She started to feel light-headed and dizzy with intermittent vision changes. She went to the emergency room and was diagnosed with a high blood sugar. She was given some fluids and advised to cut out extra sweets and resume her normal diet.

The patient has a history of osteoarthritis, atrial fibrillation, and reflux. She is doing well with her reflux on Protonix 40 mg once a day.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Reports light-headedness and dizziness.
Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or shortness of breath. Reports racing heart when anxious.
Respiratory: Denies cough, shortness of breath, or wheezing.
Gastrointestinal: Denies abdominal pain or burning with urination. Reports osteoarthritis.
Genitourinary: Denies polyuria.
Musculoskeletal: Reports osteoarthritis.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

Neck
General Examination: Neck is supple, thyroid is enlarged but non-tender.

Cardiovascular
Cardiac Examination: Irregular rate and rhythm.

Respiratory
Lung Examination: Clear bilaterally.

Gastrointestinal
Abdominal Examination: Soft abdomen with no tenderness, no hepatosplenomegaly.

Musculoskeletal
Musculoskeletal Examination: No edema in lower extremities.

RESULTS

Blood glucose is elevated. Hemoglobin A1c is elevated.

IMPRESSION

The patient is a 52-year-old female who presents for evaluation of a high blood sugar. She has an elevated blood glucose and hemoglobin A1c. She is currently on metoprolol 25 mg twice a day for atrial fibrillation. She is currently on Protonix 40 mg once a day for reflux. I have recommended metformin 500 mg twice a day for her blood glucose.

PLAN

We will send labs to work up her diabetes. I advised her to avoid foods high in sugar. I will prescribe a glucometer and instruct the nurse to teach her how to do blood sugar testing. She will continue on metoprolol 25 mg twice a day for atrial fibrillation. She will continue on Protonix 40 mg once a day for reflux.

INSTRUCTIONS

She will follow up in one week. }}<|eot_id|>
