The patient states she has been going out to eat on Friday nights and Saturday nights and has had some spicy foods or spicy shrimp. She has been experiencing abdominal pain, nausea, and diarrhea.

She reports she is starting to notice she is having bowel movements between two to three times a day on normal days. She states they are soft stools. After she has gone out and drinks with friends, she tends to have more diarrhea. She states it is usually the food, but sometimes the alcohol. She states she usually eats pasta at restaurants, such as Friday's, and the chicken alfredo. She states it normally does not bother her. She prefers to drink tequila or dark liquor, but sometimes she drinks a martini. She states it is usually the mixer they put in the drinks that bothers her. She states she has been avoiding heavy foods because of the cramping and sharp pains. She states she had some fried chicken today and it was okay.

