HISTORY OF PRESENTING ILLNESS

The patient is a pleasant 27-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for evaluation of right knee pain. The patient states that he sustained a right knee injury 3 days ago while playing soccer. He was attempting to kick the ball and felt a pop in his right knee. He notes that his knee is swollen with some of the swelling having subsided. He states that his knee does not move as well as it used to and that it feels limited. He rates his pain level between a 6 and 7 out of 10. He states that ibuprofen has helped with the pain and swelling. He reports that he can bend his knee but it hurts towards the end of motion. He also states that he can straighten his knee but it does not feel normal. He can bear weight on his leg but it feels loose.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

