VITALS

All are within normal limits.

PHYSICAL EXAM

MSK: Examination of the right knee: Significant effusion noted. Slight ecchymosis. Pain to palpation at the medial joint line. Lachman test is positive. Active range of motion is limited. Terminal extension is to 115 degrees. Flexion is to 45 degrees. Neurovascularly, bilateral lower extremities are intact. Muscle strength is 5/5.

RESULTS

X-rays of the right knee were reviewed today. They are unremarkable.

ASSESSMENT

Anterior cruciate ligament tear.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and radiographic findings today, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regards to his current symptoms. I have explained to him that his symptoms are suggestive of an anterior cruciate ligament tear. I have recommended that we obtain an MRI to evaluate the integrity of the ACL. I have also recommended that he take meloxicam 50 mg daily to reduce pain and swelling. I have also advised him to ice his knee as needed. I have also recommended that he limit his activities and use crutches when ambulating. I also advised him to refrain from jogging until further notice.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow-up with me once the results of the MRI are available. }}<|eot_id|>
