RESPIRATORY: Lungs are clear bilaterally. No wheezing, rales, or rhonchi.
SKIN: Trace edema in bilateral lower extremities.
NECK: General examination: No jugular venous distention.

RESULTS

Echocardiogram shows preserved EF of 55%, abnormal diastolic filling, and mild to moderate mitral regurgitation.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Mr. Johnson is an 82-year-old male with a past medical history significant for hypertension and stage 3 chronic kidney disease, who presents for hospital follow-up after an acute on chronic CHF exacerbation.

Acute on chronic congestive heart failure.
Medical Reasoning: This was caused by dietary indiscretion in an uncontrolled hypertension.
Medical Treatment: Continue Bumex 2 mg daily. Continue diet modification. Avoid salty foods. Weigh self daily and call if weight gain is >3 lbs in 2 days. Follow-up with nutritionist for diet education.
